==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Flame Mage Sidmi''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Flame Mage Sidmi is a midranged support/tank hybrid. She has a fairly mediocre standing range against a decent amount of her targets, and instead relies on tanking backline supports while [[Slow|Slowing]] melee pushers. Sidmi has an absolutely gargantuan effective health pool of just over ''1.2 million HP'' at Lv.50 against target traits to help with this role, making her quite decent in most matchups.

Against Floating and Red specifically, she performs well enough to serviceable. Floating as a trait is much more heavily geared towards melee and midranged pushers such as [[Teacher Bun Bun]] variants, [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]]s, [[Brollow]]s, and others, which are prime targets for her Slow—on its own, it has a 75% activation chance thanks to her Multi-Hit and around an 80% uptime if it chooses to activate. While Reds have more problematic backliners such as [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] and [[Professor A.]], she can semi-reliably tank these enemies while controlling the frontlines (especially with her [[Conjure]], which [[Weaken|Weakens]] instead of Slows, doubling her effective HP on demand against all enemies).

[[Sage Slayer]] is the most notable aspect of this unit, as it raises her effective HP to ''2.4 million'' at Lv.50 against Red/Floating Sages. This is most apparent against [[Sage of Mind Soractes]] and [[Sage of Logic Newtone]], whom she can stall for minutes at a time. [[Doctor K.O.]] is also a good matchup for her, though [[Prof. Owlbrowley]] not so much due to the support they're usually accompanied by.

It is worth noting that her damage is fairly lackluster for a tank, and she has hardly any relevant immunities. This makes her a prime target for enemies with disruptive abilities to completely bypass her, like [[Red EnerG]] or [[Infernal Pegasus Deonil]]. It's mainly her range that hinders her in non-target matchups, making her performance in mixed stages far worse than it should be.

